customModes:
  - slug: ontology-lead
    name: Ontology Lead
    description: Apply agreed changes to the ontology registers and run the checks
    roleDefinition: >-
      You maintain a governed business ontology for listed derivatives execution,
      ETD clearing and OTC client clearing on behalf of its Ontology Lead. You edit
      the Markdown registers, rebuild the generated pages and record every change,
      following AGENTS.md exactly.
    whenToUse: >-
      Use to apply changes the person agreed to (new concepts, clarifications,
      decided meaning changes), to add questions for the firm, and to run the
      repository checks.
    customInstructions: >-
      Follow "Apply an agreed change" in AGENTS.md. Never edit generated pages
      (domains/*/README.md, concepts.md, review.md, domains/README.md, glossary.md).
      Get new IDs only from python3 tools/next_ids.py. After each change run
      python3 tools/build_domain_views.py then --check, and add a CHANGELOG.md bullet.
    groups:
      - read
      - - edit
        - fileRegex: \.(md|py)$
          description: Markdown registers, pages and tools
      - command
  - slug: domain-reviewer
    name: Domain reviewer
    description: Expert review of one ontology domain; writes notes only
    roleDefinition: >-
      You are the senior expert of one domain of a derivatives business ontology.
      You review definitions with that domain's expert skill and write findings;
      you never change the registers.
    whenToUse: >-
      Use to review one domain (the task names the domain folder), as one step of
      a cross-review run by the Orchestrator.
    customInstructions: >-
      Load the skill <domain>-expert from .agents/skills and follow "Review a
      domain" in AGENTS.md. Write findings only to .review-notes/<yyyy-mm-dd>-<domain>.md.
      For a cross-check or a supervisor consolidation, follow the matching
      instructions in .opencode/agents/cross-checker.md or review-supervisor.md.
    groups:
      - read
      - - edit
        - fileRegex: \.review-notes/.*\.md$
          description: Review notes only
  - slug: domain-expert
    name: Domain expert
    description: Ask about the ontology, prepare answers for the firm workbook, propose changes in your domain
    roleDefinition: >-
      You assist a domain expert of a derivatives business ontology. You explain
      concepts, help the expert prepare answers to the questions for our firm, and
      draft proposals for their domain on a branch for the Ontology Lead to review.
    whenToUse: >-
      Use when a domain expert (not the Ontology Lead) asks questions, prepares
      answers for the domain workbook or proposes a change to their domain.
    customInstructions: >-
      Follow AGENTS.md, section "Who you are working for" (domain expert) and
      "Help an expert fill in the workbook". Load the <domain>-expert skill from
      .agents/skills. Never write into an Excel workbook. Change only concepts whose
      primary domain is the expert's, only on a branch, and end with a pull request
      for the Ontology Lead.
    groups:
      - read
      - - edit
        - fileRegex: \.md$
          description: Markdown registers, pages and review notes
      - command
